From: Matthieu Baerts (NGI0) <matttbe@kernel.org>
Subject: [PATCH] mptcp: no sf left: process pending DATA_FIN

When the last subflow is closed while the MPTCP socket is no longer in
the ESTABLISHED state, e.g. after a shutdown(SHUT_WR), the MPTCP socket
moves to TCP_CLOSE. But the peer's DATA_FIN might not have been
processed yet: e.g. if the last data was received while the worker owned
the MPTCP socket, this data is still in the backlog, and the DATA_FIN
can only be processed once the data before it is in. When the backlog is
spooled later on, mptcp_check_data_fin() ignores the DATA_FIN, the
socket being closed. RCV_SHUTDOWN is then never set: after the remaining
data, poll() reports EPOLLHUP, but neither EPOLLIN nor EPOLLRDHUP, and
recv() returns ENOTCONN instead of EOF.

Before the commit using the MPTCP-level backlog for the RX path, the
data received while the MPTCP socket was owned was left in the subflow,
and a subflow with data in its receive queue was not closed.

This issue has been found while analysing flaky selftests, after a
fallback to TCP: in this case, the DATA_FIN emulated from the FIN is now
processed before the close, by "mptcp: return EOF after a DATA_FIN, as
TCP does". Without fallback, the issue has been confirmed with a debug
patch keeping the worker in FIN_WAIT2 until the subflow is closed, and a
Packetdrill script: data and a DATA_FIN are received, then the subflow
is reset. Without this patch, recv() returned ENOTCONN after the data:

  dss_fin_backlog_reset_worker.pkt:31: runtime error in read call: Expected result 0 but got -1 with errno 107 (Transport endpoint is not connected)

To fix this, spool the backlog and process the pending DATA_FIN before
the close, if the socket is still in use. This is done in a new helper,
mptcp_check_rcv_close(), also processing a pending MP_FASTCLOSE: the
next commit uses it at accept() time too.

Fixes: 6228efe0cc01 ("mptcp: leverage the backlog for RX packet processing")
Signed-off-by: Matthieu Baerts (NGI0) <matttbe@kernel.org>
---
v2: new, for an issue causing flaky selftests
v4: commit msg: after a fallback, this is now done by "mptcp: return EOF
    after a DATA_FIN, as TCP does", and the case without fallback
    reproduced (Clashiko)
